	This release of VFORTH has a bug fix in the "f." word, and
a change to "fill". My previous posting was only marginally successful
(many systems never received it), so I am posting in its entirety, rather
than with diff's. This FORTH is my original creation, and uses
subroutine-threading and in-line code generation to improve performance.
It is written in VAX assembly code, and runs on BSD 4.2. Moving it to
other versions of VAX UNIX shouldn't be too bad, but otherwise you might
as well forget it.

				Faster than BASIC, and structured, too!
				Andy Valencia
				...!{ucbvax,fortune}!hpda!vandys
